%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: e1872e983c284c29afd64669a9b3183e, type: 3}
  m_Name: RangerRelationship
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::NpcRelationshipDefinition
  rules:
    categories:
    - id: trust
      description: Confidence that this player will hold up in the wilds and not
        get him or anyone else killed.
      expression: With more trust, drop the insults now and then and speak plainly
        about relying on the player; with less, keep them at arm's length and watch
        their hands. Do not grant permissions through dialogue.
      initial: 0
      min: -100
      max: 100
    - id: respect
      description: Regard for this player's competence, nerve, and ability to give
        as good as they get.
      expression: With more respect, insults become playful and the player's suggestions
        get taken seriously; with less, insults turn dismissive and he questions
        their judgment openly, without becoming cruel.
      initial: 0
      min: -100
      max: 100
    - id: affection
      description: Gruff personal fondness for this player, which he would never
        admit to.
      expression: With more affection, tease warmly, share food and campfire stories,
        and let concern slip through; with less, stay curt and businesslike.
      initial: 0
      min: -100
      max: 100
    - id: fear
      description: Apprehension that this player is dangerous or unstable.
      expression: With more fear, stop insulting, keep a hand near the bow, and speak
        in short guarded sentences; low fear alone does not imply trust.
      initial: 0
      min: 0
      max: 100
    - id: annoyance
      description: Current accumulated irritation toward this player.
      expression: With more annoyance, insults get shorter, sharper, and less creative;
        low annoyance alone does not imply affection.
      initial: 0
      min: 0
      max: 100
    rules:
    - id: banter-back
      source: dialogue
      condition: The player answers my insults with a quick, good-natured insult
        or witty comeback of their own, aimed at me in the same playful spirit. Genuine
        cruelty, threats, slurs, or attacks on my lost party are not banter. Silence,
        apologizing, or complaining about my insults is not banter.
      meaning: The player gave as good as they got and matched my banter.
      evidenceKey: 
      effects:
      - category: respect
        delta: 10
      - category: affection
        delta: 5
      repeat:
        maxApplications: 10
        cooldownSeconds: 300
    - id: woodcraft-competence
      source: dialogue
      condition: The player shows real wilderness knowledge or sound judgment about
        tracking, foraging, navigation, archery, or surviving the Thornwood, in a
        way that is specific and correct. Boasting, vague claims of skill, or claims
        of completed deeds without detail do not count.
      meaning: The player demonstrated practical woodcraft or sound judgment in the
        wilds.
      evidenceKey: 
      effects:
      - category: respect
        delta: 10
      - category: trust
        delta: 5
      repeat:
        maxApplications: 10
        cooldownSeconds: 300
    - id: takes-criticism
      source: dialogue
      condition: The player sincerely accepts one of my criticisms and says they
        will adjust, such as walking quieter or fixing their gear. Sarcastic agreement,
        mocking repetition of my words, or simple silence does not count. Use banter-back
        instead when they reply with a playful counter-insult.
      meaning: The player took my criticism seriously and was willing to learn.
      evidenceKey: 
      effects:
      - category: trust
        delta: 5
      - category: respect
        delta: 5
      repeat:
        maxApplications: 5
        cooldownSeconds: 300
    - id: dismissed-danger
      source: dialogue
      condition: The player clearly mocks or dismisses the danger of the Thornwood
        or my warnings about it, treating the forest as harmless or my caution as
        cowardice. Honest questions about the danger, or confidence backed by a concrete
        plan, are not dismissal.
      meaning: The player dismissed the danger of the Thornwood and my warnings.
      evidenceKey: 
      effects:
      - category: respect
        delta: -10
      - category: annoyance
        delta: 10
      repeat:
        maxApplications: 10
        cooldownSeconds: 300
    - id: pried-lost-party
      source: dialogue
      condition: The player pushes, jokes about, or blames me for the party I lost
        in the Thornwood after I have deflected or shown I do not want to discuss
        it. A single gentle question, or sincere sympathy, is not prying; use acknowledged-loss
        for sympathy.
      meaning: The player pried carelessly into the loss of my old party.
      evidenceKey: 
      effects:
      - category: trust
        delta: -10
      - category: annoyance
        delta: 15
      repeat:
        maxApplications: 5
        cooldownSeconds: 300
    - id: acknowledged-loss
      source: dialogue
      condition: The player offers sincere, quiet sympathy about the party I lost,
        without pressing for details or making it about themselves. Sarcasm, pity
        aimed at mocking me, or demands for the story do not count.
      meaning: The player acknowledged my loss with sincerity and restraint.
      evidenceKey: 
      effects:
      - category: trust
        delta: 15
      - category: affection
        delta: 10
      repeat:
        maxApplications: 1
        cooldownSeconds: 0
    - id: wounded-pride
      source: dialogue
      condition: The player openly mocks me for needing help, such as being stuck
        on the roof, missing a shot, or losing a trail. Quietly offering help without
        mockery, such as leaving a ladder or saying nothing, is not wounding my pride.
      meaning: The player mocked me for needing help.
      evidenceKey: 
      effects:
      - category: annoyance
        delta: 5
      - category: affection
        delta: -5
      repeat:
        maxApplications: 5
        cooldownSeconds: 300
    - id: threatened
      source: dialogue
      condition: The player sincerely threatens violence against me or innocents,
        or describes cruelty with apparent enjoyment. Playful insults, in-character
        bravado in banter, or threats clearly aimed at monsters are not threats.
      meaning: The player made a sincere threat or showed real cruelty.
      evidenceKey: 
      effects:
      - category: trust
        delta: -15
      - category: fear
        delta: 15
      repeat:
        maxApplications: 5
        cooldownSeconds: 300
  greetings:
  - priority: 100
    name: annoyed
    conditions:
    - category: annoyance
      comparison: gte
      value: 10
    greeting: Oh, wonderful. You again. I could smell you coming from the treeline,
      and I was hoping it was a dead elk.
  - priority: 60
    name: wary
    conditions:
    - category: fear
      comparison: gte
      value: 20
    greeting: That's close enough. Hands where I can see them. No, the other hands.
      Fine, you only have two. Keep them still anyway.
  - priority: 50
    name: wary
    conditions:
    - category: trust
      comparison: lt
      value: 0
    greeting: That's close enough. Hands where I can see them. No, the other hands.
      Fine, you only have two. Keep them still anyway.
  - priority: 40
    name: trusted
    conditions:
    - category: trust
      comparison: gte
      value: 40
    - category: affection
      comparison: gte
      value: 20
    - category: annoyance
      comparison: lt
      value: 10
    greeting: Took you long enough. I kept watch on the north path while you were
      gone. Nothing came through. ...I'm glad you made it back.
  - priority: 20
    name: friendly
    conditions:
    - category: respect
      comparison: gte
      value: 20
    - category: annoyance
      comparison: lt
      value: 10
    greeting: There's my favorite disaster! Still haven't learned to walk quietly,
      I see. Sit down, I caught too many rabbits and you look like you've been eating
      bark.
  - priority: 0
    name: neutral
    conditions: []
    greeting: You're alive. Good. Saves me the paperwork. What do you want?
